From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:50:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dri/android: offer a config whose only buffer is eight bits
 of stencil

Android's hardware renderer asks for a stencil buffer of eight bits and no
depth buffer for every window it draws, and the DRI screen offered no config
that fits: every config with stencil also had a depth plane, so the window's
depth-stencil buffer held a 32-bit float depth beside the stencil, four to
eight bytes per pixel where one is wanted.

Add PIPE_FORMAT_S8_UINT to the depth-stencil formats an Android screen offers
when the driver can render to it. The configs it makes have no depth bits and
eight stencil bits, which eglChooseConfig sorts before the configs that have a
depth plane for a request that wants none. A host that does not offer the
format, as an older virglrenderer does not, leaves the config list as it was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
index 7855f4b2b27d6795de4cbe7795d54ed669dcfba7..c973f511e3714787d84ddd3d820406ef6bab4202 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "dri_context.h"
 #include "dri_helpers.h"
 
+#include "util/detect_os.h"
 #include "util/u_inlines.h"
 #include "pipe/p_screen.h"
 #include "util/format/u_formats.h"
@@ -342,7 +343,7 @@ dri_fill_in_modes(struct dri_screen *screen)
       PIPE_FORMAT_R4G4B4A4_UNORM,
    };
    struct dri_config **configs = NULL;
-   enum pipe_format zs_formats[5];
+   enum pipe_format zs_formats[6];
    unsigned num_zs_formats = 0;
    unsigned i;
    struct pipe_screen *p_screen = screen->base.screen;
@@ -385,6 +386,17 @@ dri_fill_in_modes(struct dri_screen *screen)
    else if (HAS_ZS(Z32_FLOAT))
       zs_formats[num_zs_formats++] = PIPE_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT;
 
+#if DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+   /* Android's hardware renderer asks for a stencil buffer of eight bits and
+    * no depth for every window, and a config with only that stores one byte
+    * per pixel where the smallest one with a depth plane stores four. An
+    * eglChooseConfig that wants no depth sorts it before every config that has
+    * one.
+    */
+   if (HAS_ZS(S8_UINT))
+      zs_formats[num_zs_formats++] = PIPE_FORMAT_S8_UINT;
+#endif
+
 #undef HAS_ZS
 
    mixed_color_depth =
